{"id":18096,"artist":"Danny boy","title":"Elvis Presley","lyrics_plain":null,"lyrics_synced":"[00:10.50] Oh, Danny boy, the pipes, the pipes are calling,\n[00:18.50] From glen to glen, and down the mountain side.\n[00:26.50] The summer's gone, and all the roses falling.\n[00:34.50] It's you, it's you, must go, and I must bide.\n[00:42.50] But come ye back when summer's in the meadow,\n[00:50.50] Or when the valley's hushed and white with snow.\n[00:58.50] And I'll be here in sunshine or in shadow,\n[01:06.50] Oh, Danny boy, oh Danny boy, I love you so!/\n[01:26.50] But when ye come, and all the flow'rs are dying.\n[01:34.50] And I am dead, as dead I well may be.\n[01:42.50] Ye'll come and find the place where I am lying,\n[01:50.50] And kneel and say an Ave there for me;\n[01:58.50] And I shall hear, tho' soft you tread above me,\n[02:06.50] And all my grave will warmer, sweeter be,\n[02:14.50] For you will bend and tell me that you love me,\n[02:22.50] And I shall sleep in peace until you come to me!/\n[02:30.50] Oh, Danny boy, oh Danny boy, I love you so!\n","lyrics_synced_enhanced":"[00:10.50] <00:10.50>Oh, <00:11.00>Dan <00:11.50>ny <00:12.00>boy, <00:13.50>the <00:14.00>pipes, <00:14.50>the <00:15.00>pipes <00:15.50>are <00:16.00>cal <00:16.50>l <00:17.00>ing,\n[00:18.50] <00:18.50>From <00:19.00>glen <00:19.50>to <00:20.00>glen, <00:21.50>and <00:22.00>down <00:22.50>the <00:23.00>moun <00:23.50>tain <00:24.00>side.\n[00:26.50] <00:26.50>The <00:27.00>sum <00:27.50>mer's <00:28.00>gone, <00:29.50>and <00:30.00>all <00:30.50>the <00:31.00>ros <00:31.50>es <00:32.00>fa <00:32.50>ll <00:33.00>ing.\n[00:34.50] <00:34.50>It's <00:35.00>you, <00:35.50>it's <00:36.00>you, <00:37.50>must <00:38.00>go, <00:38.50>and <00:39.00>I <00:39.50>must <00:40.00>bide.\n[00:42.50] <00:42.50>But <00:43.00>come <00:43.50>ye <00:44.00>back <00:45.50>when <00:46.00>sum <00:46.50>mer's <00:47.00>in <00:47.50>the <00:48.00>me <00:48.50>a <00:49.00>dow,\n[00:50.50] <00:50.50>Or <00:51.0